4. NAMING CONVENTION STANDARDS
AI-code chaos se bachne ke liye strict naming required.

Layer	Convention	Example
Database tables	snake_case, plural	users, supplier_offers, order_items
Database columns	snake_case	created_at, segment_id, is_active
Prisma models	PascalCase, singular	User, SupplierOffer, OrderItem
TypeScript types	PascalCase	CreateOrderDto, ProductResponse
TypeScript variables	camelCase	orderItem, supplierId
API routes	kebab-case	/api/v1/orders, /api/v1/products
Functions	camelCase	createOrder, updateInventory
Constants	UPPER_SNAKE_CASE	MAX_RETRY_COUNT, DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE
Enums	PascalCase	OrderStatus, SegmentType
DTOs	PascalCase + Dto suffix	CreateOrderDto, UpdateProductDto
Rules:

Singular for entity names, plural for tables
No abbreviations (user not usr, product not prod)
No mixed naming (do not use userId and user_id interchangeably)
AI code must follow these strictly
5. ERROR HANDLING PHILOSOPHY
Standardized error format for all APIs.

API Error Format
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Product quantity must be greater than 0",
    "field": "quantity",
    "details": []
  },
  "requestId": "req_abc123xyz"
}
Validation Error Format
{
  "success": false,
  "error": {
    "code": "VALIDATION_ERROR",
    "message": "Invalid input data",
    "fields": {
      "quantity": "Must be greater than 0",
      "price": "Must be a positive number"
    }
  }
}
Error Severity Levels
Level	Action
FATAL	Log + Alert + Stop execution
ERROR	Log + Alert + Return 500
WARNING	Log + Do not alert
INFO	Log only
DEBUG	Log in dev only
Retry Policies
Scenario	Max Retries	Backoff Strategy
Payment processing	3	Exponential (1s, 2s, 4s)
Shipment tracking	5	Exponential
Notification delivery	3	Linear (2s, 2s, 2s)
Inventory sync	2	Exponential
External API calls	3	Exponential + jitter
Retry only idempotent operations.

6. IDEMPOTENCY RULES
Critical for:

Payments
Order status updates
Shipment retries
Webhook processing
Inventory adjustments
Implementation
Every write endpoint accepting external input must support:

Idempotency key header: Idempotency-Key
Prisma upsert where applicable
Transaction boundaries
Duplicate request detection
Example:

// Orders service
async createOrder(data, idempotencyKey) {
  // Check if already processed
  const existing = await this.prisma.order.findUnique({
    where: { idempotencyKey }
  });
  
  if (existing) {
    return existing; // Return same response
  }
  
  // Proceed with transaction
  return this.prisma.$transaction(async (tx) => {
    // Create order
    // Update inventory
    // Create payment
    // All in one atomic transaction
  });
}
7. API CONTRACT STANDARDS
Response Envelope Format
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { },
  "meta": {
    "page": 1,
    "perPage": 20,
    "total": 100,
    "totalPages": 5
  }
}
Pagination Standard
{
  "page": 1,
  "perPage": 20,
  "sortBy": "createdAt",
  "sortOrder": "desc",
  "filters": {
    "segmentId": "TEXTILE",
    "status": "ACTIVE"
  }
}
Filtering Standard
URL query params:

?segmentId=TEXTILE&status=ACTIVE&minPrice=100&maxPrice=500
Sorting Standard
?sortBy=createdAt&sortOrder=desc
Validation Rules
All inputs validated via Zod schemas
Type-safe request/response DTOs
Consistent error messages
No raw database errors exposed
8. SOFT DELETE POLICY
Soft Delete (enable)
Entity	Reason
users	Audit trail, historical orders
buyers	Business records, tax compliance
suppliers	Order history, audit
products	Order history, past references
orders	Financial records, legal
payments	Financial audit trail
invoices	Tax compliance
Hard Delete (prohibited for)
Users
Buyers
Suppliers
Orders
Payments
Invoices
Shipments
Returns
Allowed Hard Delete
Entity	Reason
draft quotes	Temporary, not committed
test data	Development only
temp media	Unreferenced uploads
failed job logs	After retention period
Implementation
All entities have:

deleted_at TIMESTAMP NULL
Queries must filter:

WHERE deleted_at IS NULL
Admin-only "include deleted" option.

9. DATA RETENTION POLICY
Data Type	Retention	Action After
Order records	7 years	Archive
Payment records	7 years	Archive
Audit logs	3 years	Archive
Search logs	2 years	Delete
Session data	30 days	Delete
OTP records	7 days	Delete
Failed job logs	30 days	Delete
Temp media	30 days	Delete
Notification logs	1 year	Archive
System logs	1 year	Archive
Archive = Move to cold storage

10. CONCURRENCY STRATEGY
Critical for:

Inventory
Procurement
Order processing
Payment processing
Optimistic Locking
version INTEGER DEFAULT 1

UPDATE products 
SET quantity = quantity - 1, version = version + 1
WHERE id = ? AND version = ?
If version mismatch → retry or abort.

Inventory Locking
SELECT quantity FROM inventory WHERE id = ? FOR UPDATE
Within transaction.

Payment Locking
SELECT status FROM payments WHERE id = ? FOR UPDATE
Prevent double-processing.

Rules
Always use transactions for multi-table writes
Always check version for optimistic locking
Always release locks quickly
Never hold locks across API boundaries
Always retry with exponential backoff
